          "path": "_m/u/3/3/d/ddr-museum-wp/20190722-105208-stasi-room-in-.jpg",
          "filename": "20190722 105208 Stasi room in DDR Museum.jpg",
          "caption": "Stasi room in DDR Museum. The two-track TG7127 cassette decks were developed (apparently for telephone tapping) and built at the Institut für Technische Untersuchungen (ITU) in Beucha in the 1980s[1]. Their Soviet counterparts were deliberately made incompatible with plain cassette recorders, and this East German decks were probably incompatible, too.",
